      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "David Cronenberg's early body horror masterpiece Rabid established his signature blend of biological terror and social commentary. Following his debut <a href=\"/movie/27429\" class=\"movie-title\">Shivers</a> (1975), Cronenberg cast adult film star Marilyn Chambers as Rose, a motorcycle crash victim who develops a vampiric appetite after experimental skin graft surgery. The film's exploration of medical manipulation and viral outbreak predates similar themes in <a href=\"/movie/9426\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9426\">The Fly</a> (1986) and <a href=\"/movie/837\" class=\"movie-title\">Videodrome</a> (1983), showcasing Cronenberg's emerging obsession with body transformation and technological intervention."
      },
      {
